{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Patchset 2 pushed — `make verify` GREEN on a quiescent tree\n\n```\n19844 passed, 80 skipped, 14 warnings in 2457.60s (0:40:57)\nmake verify rc=0\n```\n\nZero failures and zero errors, against the amended tree with no commits made during the run — so\nneither of the two problems in the first attempt recurs: the sibling-import defect is fixed, and\nthe seven `repo HEAD moved during this test` errors were entirely my own procedural fault and are\ngone now that the tree was quiescent.\n\nChange **2689**, patchset 2, https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2689 — `Change-Id`\ncarried forward (`git commit --amend --no-edit`, so it is a new patchset on the SAME change, not\na duplicate). Trailers verified: `rebar-ticket: a68c-9633-248c-4b06`,\n`Signed-off-by: RebarBotNava`, and `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` resolves it.\n\n**Vote state at push time: `LLM-Review` no vote, `Verified` no vote, status NEW.** Not submitted.\nNote that the Gerrit host REBOOTED at ~23:52 UTC (it was briefly unreachable — `curl` refused,\n`git ls-remote` reset), so patchset 1 may not have been picked up by the review bot at all; this\npatchset should re-trigger both gates cleanly.\n\n## One limitation of the guard I am recording rather than leaving implicit\n\n`scripts/check_user_data_size.py` compares the DECODED transport bytes (the gzip payload) against\n16,384, on the basis that EC2's UserData limit applies to the raw data before base64 encoding.\nI established that framing from the AWS documented limit plus the fact that the plan now\ngenerates — **I did not read the provider's validator source for `user_data_base64`.** If the\nprovider ALSO caps the base64 STRING at 16,384, there is a band — gzip between 12,288 and 16,384\nbytes — where the guard would pass something terraform rejects.\n\nThat band is unreachable today by a wide margin: the payload is 6,941 gzip bytes, 5,347 bytes\nbelow the bottom of it. But it is a real gap in the guard's claim, not a hypothetical one, and\nchecking both quantities is a two-line change. Recording it here rather than fixing it in this\npatchset, because the change is already `Verified`-pending and this is not a defect in anything\nthat ships today."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788652974947920001,"uuid":"85b687bb-0e4e-46da-90ad-485aae01dac9"}